OL,3,GNEWSA'We are making opera that looks
OL,4,Aand sounds like Bradford'
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt has been sung around the globe in
OL,7,Fmultiple languages and voted the
OL,8,Fgreatest opera of all time, but The
OL,9,FMarriage of Figaro has never been
OL,10,Fperformed in a Bradford accent - until
OL,11,Fnow.
OL,13,FTranslated into Yorkshire dialect by
OL,14,Fpoet Ian McMillan, reorchestrated by
OL,15,FBen Crick and directed by Alex
OL,16,FChisholm, the Mozart classic has been
OL,17,Freinvented for the third Bradford Opera
OL,18,FFestival.
OL,23,APub: 14-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
